    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite efficiency score of 80.43. While he faces a slight efficiency tax due to the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time, the combination of his spot in the three-hole and a favorable matchup against Mahle makes him our most bankable asset. **Mickey Moniak** follows closely at 75.75, benefiting significantly from a platoon advantage and a high-impact spot in the order. We are also leaning into **Max Muncy** (68.41) and **Seiya Suzuki** (66.22), both of whom capitalize on high SP_xERA matchups against Lauer and Canning, respectively, to drive our power metrics against vulnerable arms.\n\nPlatoon edges are the primary catalyst for our lineup construction today. **Henry Bolte** (65.40) is a high-upside play at the top of the order, leveraging a 17% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s profile and a park factor shift, while **Isaac Paredes** (62.00) gains significant ground against Matthews. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Cole Young**, whose 46.51 score kept him in the conversation until the final iteration. Ultimately, **Cole Young** was squeezed out because his offensive upside against Johnson didn't provide the same category-specific urgency\u2014specifically regarding SB potential\u2014that our starters like **Zach McKinstry** (48.41) offer, even despite the latter's lower base projection.\n\nWe remain vigilant regarding risks, particularly with **Zach McKinstry** and **James Wood**, both of whom are facing pitchers with sub-3.80 xERAs. While **James Wood** boasts an impressive 0.392 xwOBA, his score of 62.24 is suppressed slightly by an elite holding pitcher, which may dampen his stolen base utility today. Across the board, ensure lineup monitors are active for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**; while their projections are solid, their status could shift if weather reports or late-scratch notifications materialize in their respective parks. We are effectively capped today, so every point of efficiency from **Kyle Karros** and **Brice Turang** must be squeezed out to maintain our 5x5 pace.",
